{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Who pant</b> — the meaning is תשאפו. When will you drag the heads of the poor upon the dust of the earth? Enough for them is their lowliness." "<b>And turn aside the way of the humble</b> — from the path of uprightness which is their path, until they removed humility from Israel, until no man is ashamed to go with his father to the same girl."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Reads השואפים as from root א-ש-ף with implied second-person address; תשאפו kept in Hebrew as Ibn Ezra's grammatical reinterpretation.", 1 "The phrase עם אביו עם נערה is hyper-literally 'with his father with a girl'; Ibn Ezra appears to allude to shared sexual access, but the syntax is compressed and left untranslated beyond the literal."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:17:50.524670363Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}